 0.01, indicating that the assumption of independent errors was violated.", "keywords": ["significant autocorrelation"], "direction": "significant", "effect_strength": "strong", "hedging": false, "claim": "The Ljung-Box test revealed significant autocorrelation, indicating that the assumption of independent errors was violated."}], "primary_direction": "significant", "has_cross_section_conflict": false, "any_hedging": false, "sections": ["results"]}, {"test_type": "r", "statistic_value": -0.62, "df1": 247.0, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.001, "p_equality": "<", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "r(247) = -0.62, p < 0.001", "textual_interpretation": "a strong negative relationship, suggesting that firms with higher debt burdens experienced significantly lower profitability margins", "interpretation_direction": "significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "bivariate correlation between long-term debt ratios and net profit margins", "interpretations": [{"section": "results", "sentence": "The analysis revealed a strong negative relationship, r(247) = -0.62, p < 0.001, suggesting that firms with higher debt burdens experienced significantly lower profitability margins.", "keywords": ["strong negative relationship", "significantly lower"], "direction": "significant", "effect_strength": "strong", "hedging": false, "claim": "There was a strong negative correlation between long-term debt ratios and net profit margins, indicating that firms with higher debt burdens had significantly lower profitability margins."}], "primary_direction": "significant", "has_cross_section_conflict": false, "any_hedging": false, "sections": ["results"]}], "verified_tests": [{"test_type": "Q", "statistic_value": 45.07, "df1": 20.0, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.01, "p_equality": "<", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "Q(20) = 45.07, p < 0.01", "textual_interpretation": "significant autocorrelation, indicating that the assumption of independent errors was violated", "interpretation_direction": "significan