native Responses Scale and post-intervention depressive symptoms measured by the Beck Depression Inventory-II."}], "merged_tests": [{"test_type": "chi", "statistic_value": 4.82, "df1": 11.0, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.9396, "p_equality": "=", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "χ²(11) = 4.82, p = 0.9396", "textual_interpretation": "no significant differences in categorical variables such as employment status and marital status across conditions", "interpretation_direction": "not_significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "Demographic characteristics and baseline psychological measures were examined across the five intervention groups to assess randomization success.", "interpretations": [{"section": "results", "sentence": "A chi-square test of independence revealed no significant differences in categorical variables such as employment status and marital status across conditions, χ²(11) = 4.82, p = 0.9396, indicating that randomization was effective and groups were comparable at baseline.", "keywords": ["no significant differences"], "direction": "not_significant", "effect_strength": "none", "hedging": false, "claim": "The chi-square test indicated that there were no significant differences in categorical variables across conditions, confirming effective randomization."}], "primary_direction": "not_significant", "has_cross_section_conflict": false, "any_hedging": false, "sections": ["results"]}, {"test_type": "Q", "statistic_value": 42.49, "df1": 24.0, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.011, "p_equality": "=", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "Q(24) = 42.49, p = 0.011", "textual_interpretation": "significant heterogeneity among studies", "interpretation_direction": "significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "Heterogeneity analysis using Cochran's Q statistic was conducted to evaluate consistency of effect sizes across the 25 included studies in our meta-analysis of cognitive-behavioral interventions for social anxiety.", "interpretations": [{"section": "results", "sentence": "The Q-statistic indicated significant heterogeneity among studies, Q(24) = 42.49, p = 0.011, suggesting that effect sizes varied substantially across investigations.", "keywords": ["significant heterogeneity"], "direction": "significant", "effect_strength": "strong", "hedging": false, "claim": "The Q-statistic showed significant heterogeneity among studies, indicating substantial variation in effect sizes."}], "primary_direction": "significant", "has_cross_section_conflict": false, "any_hedging": false, "sections": ["results"]}, {"test_type": "r", "statistic_value": 0.2, "df1": 172.0, "df2": null, "reported_p": 0.01, "p_equality": "<", "two_tailed": true, "raw_text": "r(172) = 0.2, p < 0.01", "textual_interpretation": "higher baseline rumination was significantly associated with greater depressive symptoms following treatment", "interpretation_direction": "significant", "consistent": true, "notes": "Pearson correlation analysis of the 172 participants with complete data on both measures between baseline rumination scores on the Ruminative Responses Scale and post-intervention depressive symptoms measured by the Beck Depression Inventory-II.", "interpretations": [{"section": "results", "sentence": "A Pearson correlation analysis of the 172 participants with complete data on both measures revealed a modest positive correlation, r(172) = 0.2, p < 0.01, indicating that higher baseline rumination was significantly associated with greater depressive symptoms following treatment.", "keywords": ["modest positive correlation", "significantly associated"], "direction": "significant", "effect_strength": "weak", "hedging": false, "claim": "The Pearson correlation analysis found a modest positive correlation between baseline rumination and post-intervention depressive symptoms, indicating a significant but small effect."}, {"section": "results", "sentence": "Although statistically significant, the effect size was small, suggesting that while rumination contributes to post-int